{"step_index":99,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-13T19:46:15Z","content":"Priyanshu, all 3 research agents finished and the full report is in the artifact above. Here's the ultra-short version:\n\n**If you want NEW + AppleCare → Unicorn Store clearance deals.** Previous-gen sealed MacBook Pros at 25-35% off. A 16\" M1 Max 32GB/1TB is ₹2,14,435 (was ₹3,29,900). Full Apple warranty, AppleCare eligible, stack HDFC/HSBC card for more off.\n\n**If budget matters more than AppleCare → Sahivalue or Cashify.** M1 Pro 32GB for ₹1,10,000–₹1,35,000. No AppleCare possible (60-day original purchase rule kills it), but you get 6-month seller warranty.\n\n**If you want the LONGEST warranty on used → CeX India.** 2-year warranty, 60+ physical stores to inspect before buying.\n\n**What doesn't work:**\n- Apple Certified Refurbished Store **doesn't exist in India** (404 error)\n- Back Market / Reebelo **don't ship to India**\n- AppleCare+ on any used Mac **older than 60 days from original purchase = permanently ineligible**\n\nTwo key things that might change your decision:\n1. The M1 Pro/Max are still genuinely fast chips — \"previous gen\" doesn't mean slow\n2. If AppleCare is a hard requirement, refurbished is basically ruled out — go with Unicorn's sealed clearance stock instead"}
