{"step_index":110,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-14T07:47:51Z","content":"Priyanshu, **no, you absolutely cannot share Final Cut Pro with a Windows user. There is no way to do this.**\n\nHere is exactly why:\n\n1. **It does not work on Windows:** Final Cut Pro is built exclusively for macOS. Apple has never made a Windows version, and a Windows computer literally cannot install or run the software.\n2. **It is not a subscription:** It is a one-time digital license that gets permanently tied to your personal Apple ID. You don't get a serial key that you can just hand to a friend. \n\n**How sharing actually works:**\nYou can only share Final Cut Pro with someone who **also owns a Mac**. To do this, you have to add their Apple ID to your Apple \"Family Sharing\" group (you can share purchases with up to 5 family members). Once they are in your Family Sharing group, they can open the Mac App Store on their own MacBook and download Final Cut Pro for free. \n\nIf your friend is on a Windows PC, buying this will not help them at all. If you both need to collaborate on video editing across Mac and Windows, you should look into Adobe Premiere Pro or DaVinci Resolve, as both work on both operating systems.","thinking":"**Assessing the Inquiry**\n\nOkay, I'm breaking down the user's question. It seems they want to share a subscription, likely for Final Cut Pro, with someone using Windows. My initial focus is to clarify the scope of the request: Is subscription sharing permitted, and if not, are there any workarounds?\n\n\n**Clarifying the Subscription**\n\nI've clarified the nature of the \"subscription\"—it's a one-time purchase tied to an Apple ID, not a recurring subscription. Sharing is limited to Apple's Family Sharing or authorizing another Mac with the purchasing Apple ID. Most importantly, it's macOS only; Final Cut Pro will not work on Windows because of OS-specific components. No workarounds exist. A hackintosh or VM is not a practical solution.\n\n\n"}
